Below is a practical, step‑by‑step blueprint for building a modern, production‑ready frontend for an e‑commerce site.  
Feel free to skip sections that you already know, or dive deeper into the parts that match your stack.

---

## 1. Planning & Design

| Step | What to do | Why |
|------|------------|-----|
| **Define core features** | Product catalog, search, filters, cart, checkout, user accounts, reviews, admin panel, analytics | Keeps scope focused |
| **Create wireframes** | Use Figma/Sketch/Adobe XD | Visualise layout before coding |
| **Design a UI kit / design system** | Colors, typography, spacing, components | Consistency & reusability |
| **Plan responsive breakpoints** | Mobile‑first, then tablet, desktop | Works on all devices |
| **Accessibility audit** | WCAG 2.1 AA | Inclusive UX & SEO |

---

## 2. Choose a Tech Stack

| Category | Options | Recommendation |
|----------|---------|----------------|
| **Framework** | React, Vue, Angular, Svelte | **React** (most community) |
| **State mgmt** | Redux Toolkit, Zustand, Recoil, Context API | **Redux Toolkit** (scalable) |
| **Styling** | Tailwind CSS, Styled‑Components, CSS Modules | **Tailwind** (utility‑first) |
| **Routing** | React Router, Next.js (SSR) | **Next.js** (SSR + SSG) |
| **Data fetching** | React Query, SWR, Apollo Client | **React Query** (REST) |
| **Auth** | NextAuth, Auth0, Firebase Auth | **NextAuth** (JWT + OAuth) |
| **Payments** | Stripe, PayPal, Braintree | **Stripe** (API‑first) |
| **Testing** | Jest + React Testing Library, Cypress | Unit + E2E |
| **CI/CD** | GitHub Actions, GitLab CI, CircleCI | GitHub Actions (free for public) |
| **Deployment** | Vercel, Netlify, AWS Amplify | **Vercel** (Next.js) |

> **Tip:** If you need SEO for product pages, use Next.js with static generation (`getStaticProps`) or server‑side rendering (`getServerSideProps`).

---

